    "title": "Moses Spoke to Pharaoh-But Feared His Own Voice - NewsBreak",
    "text": "3 days ago Photo by Chat GPT Moses confronted the most powerful ruler on earth. He challenged slavery. He announced plagues. He demanded freedom. History remembers him as fearless. But Scripture shows a different picture. Moses repeatedly told God, “I am slow of speech. I can’t talk.”\nPublicly, he looked confident. Privately, he felt inadequate. He depended on Aaron. He doubted himself. Even while performing miracles, he struggled with insecurity. Calling didn’t erase weakness.\nBible Vod taught me that God doesn’t wait for confidence. He works through dependence. Moses never became a great speaker. He became a great listener. Faith isn’t about sounding strong. It’s about trusting God’s voice more than your own fear.\n58",
